    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Data collected by the University of California at Riverside (UCR), the California Division of Mines and Geology (CDMG), the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS), and others have been compiled to create a data set consisting of 7,447 stations on the Santa Ana 1° by 2° quadrangle. A listing of these data by source is on the diskette (Part B) accompanying this report. This report supplements The Complete Bouguer gravity anomaly map of the Santa Ana 1 ° by 2° quadrangle, California by Biehler and others (1992). Descriptions, coordinates, and observed gravity values for 39 base stations have been included. Locations of the data sets and a color Bouguer anomaly map contoured at an interval of 10 mGal are included.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
